{"book_id": "physics-form-four-syllabus-unconfirmed-efa0b6eda0ac", "source_sha256": "efa0b6eda0ac6e3edc18f649a4dba453a61ec010eaf6e7946d1eed77e8caaec7", "pages": [{"pdf_page": 11, "transcribed": true, "surfaces": [{"printed_page": "4", "printed_page_status": "observed", "printed_page_system": "arabic", "render_size_px": [1240, 1754], "elements": [{"key": "header", "type": "running_header", "bbox": [195, 25, 475, 60], "text": "Physics for Secondary Schools"}, {"key": "relation", "type": "paragraph", "bbox": [132, 117, 610, 151], "text": "relation,"}, {"key": "speed", "type": "math", "bbox": [218, 150, 360, 206], "payload": {"latex": "v=\\frac{\\lambda}{T}"}}, {"key": "but", "type": "paragraph", "bbox": [133, 247, 610, 313], "text": "But \\(f=\\tfrac{1}{T}\\)"}, {"key": "therefore", "type": "paragraph", "bbox": [133, 350, 610, 385], "text": "Therefore, \\(v=\\lambda f\\)."}, {"key": "ex1", "type": "heading", "bbox": [205, 429, 380, 470], "text": "Example 1.1", "payload": {"level": 3, "role": "other"}}, {"key": "q1", "type": "example", "bbox": [147, 487, 610, 625], "text": "Determine the amplitude, period and frequency of the wave represented in the displacement-time graph shown in Figure 1.4."}, {"key": "graph1", "type": "figure", "bbox": [140, 648, 600, 887], "crop": {"kind": "graph", "dpi": 150, "printed_label": "Figure 1.4", "description": "Displacement-time graph, amplitude 0.5 m and period 0.2 s."}}, {"key": "cap1", "type": "caption", "bbox": [329, 902, 450, 928], "text": "**Figure 1.4**", "payload": {"target_refs": ["@graph1"]}}, {"key": "s1", "type": "heading", "bbox": [158, 947, 610, 986], "text": "Solution", "payload": {"level": 4, "role": "other"}}, {"key": "amp", "type": "solution", "bbox": [158, 999, 610, 1100], "text": "The maximum position is measured from equilibrium 0 to \\(0.5\\,\\mathrm{m}\\). Therefore, amplitude of the wave is \\(0.5\\,\\mathrm{m}\\)."}, {"key": "period", "type": "solution", "bbox": [158, 1120, 610, 1289], "text": "The period of the wave, is the time taken to complete one cycle. In Figure 1.4, the time taken to complete one cycle is \\(0.2\\,\\mathrm{s}\\). Therefore, the period is \\(0.2\\,\\mathrm{s}\\)."}, {"key": "freqintro", "type": "solution", "bbox": [171, 1298, 610, 1357], "text": "The frequency of the wave is given by:"}, {"key": "freq1", "type": "math", "bbox": [212, 1370, 610, 1445], "payload": {"latex": "f=\\frac{1}{T}"}}, {"key": "freq2", "type": "math", "bbox": [215, 1452, 610, 1531], "payload": {"latex": "f=\\frac{1}{0.2\\,\\mathrm{s}}"}}, {"key": "freq3", "type": "math", "bbox": [217, 1543, 610, 1578], "payload": {"latex": "f=5\\,\\mathrm{Hz}."}}, {"key": "ex2", "type": "heading", "bbox": [720, 117, 920, 163], "text": "Example 1.2", "payload": {"level": 3, "role": "other"}}, {"key": "q2", "type": "example", "bbox": [659, 171, 1125, 342], "text": "The displacement-distance graph corresponding to a wave in example 1.1 is shown in Figure 1.5. Use the graph to determine the wavelength and velocity of the wave."}, {"key": "graph2", "type": "figure", "bbox": [648, 350, 1130, 613], "crop": {"kind": "graph", "dpi": 150, "printed_label": "Figure 1.5", "description": "Displacement-distance graph with wavelength 2 m."}}, {"key": "cap2", "type": "caption", "bbox": [830, 618, 985, 644], "text": "**Figure 1.5**", "payload": {"target_refs": ["@graph2"]}}, {"key": "s2", "type": "heading", "bbox": [661, 668, 1122, 701], "text": "Solution", "payload": {"level": 4, "role": "other"}}, {"key": "wl", "type": "solution", "bbox": [661, 706, 1122, 805], "text": "From the graph, the wavelength is the distance between two successive crests and its value is \\(2\\,\\mathrm{m}\\)."}, {"key": "velintro", "type": "solution", "bbox": [661, 820, 1122, 854], "text": "The velocity of the wave, \\(v\\) is given by:"}, {"key": "vel1", "type": "math", "bbox": [670, 855, 1122, 888], "payload": {"latex": "v=f\\lambda"}}, {"key": "vel2", "type": "math", "bbox": [670, 895, 1122, 929], "payload": {"latex": "v=5\\,\\mathrm{Hz}\\times2\\,\\mathrm{m}"}}, {"key": "vel3", "type": "math", "bbox": [670, 947, 1122, 986], "payload": {"latex": "v=10\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-1}}"}}, {"key": "ex3", "type": "heading", "bbox": [720, 999, 920, 1044], "text": "Example 1.3", "payload": {"level": 3, "role": "other"}}, {"key": "q3", "type": "example", "bbox": [670, 1050, 1137, 1150], "text": "What is the wavelength of a wave whose speed is \\(4\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-1}}\\) and frequency is \\(2\\,\\mathrm{Hz}\\)?"}, {"key": "s3", "type": "heading", "bbox": [670, 1175, 1137, 1208], "text": "Solution", "payload": {"level": 4, "role": "other"}}, {"key": "speed3", "type": "solution", "bbox": [670, 1210, 1137, 1254], "text": "Speed, \\(v=4\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-1}}\\)"}, {"key": "frequency3", "type": "solution", "bbox": [670, 1258, 1137, 1289], "text": "Frequency, \\(f=2\\,\\mathrm{Hz}=2\\,\\mathrm{s^{-1}}\\)"}, {"key": "then", "type": "solution", "bbox": [670, 1298, 1137, 1330], "text": "Then from,"}, {"key": "eq3", "type": "math", "bbox": [740, 1330, 1137, 1360], "payload": {"latex": "v=f\\lambda"}}, {"key": "thus3", "type": "solution", "bbox": [670, 1370, 1137, 1445], "text": "Thus, \\(\\lambda=\\tfrac{v}{f}\\)"}, {"key": "eq4", "type": "math", "bbox": [770, 1452, 1137, 1531], "payload": {"latex": "=\\frac{4\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-1}}}{2\\,\\mathrm{s^{-1}}}"}}, {"key": "eq5", "type": "math", "bbox": [770, 1543, 1137, 1578], "payload": {"latex": "=2\\,\\mathrm{m}."}}, {"key": "number", "type": "page_number", "bbox": [190, 1617, 235, 1660], "text": "4"}]}]}], "exclusions": [{"pdf_page": 11, "surface_id": "s-p0011-01", "bbox_pt": [484.8619032258065, 810.8235193548386, 576.0735483870967, 829.0658483870967], "reason": "acquisition_noise", "description": "CamScanner watermark."}], "groups": [{"key": "g_ex1", "kind": "example", "title": "Example 1.1", "element_refs": ["@ex1", "@q1", "@graph1", "@cap1", "@s1", "@amp", "@period", "@freqintro", "@freq1", "@freq2", "@freq3"]}, {"key": "g_ex2", "kind": "example", "title": "Example 1.2", "element_refs": ["@ex2", "@q2", "@graph2", "@cap2", "@s2", "@wl", "@velintro", "@vel1", "@vel2", "@vel3"]}, {"key": "g_ex3", "kind": "example", "title": "Example 1.3", "element_refs": ["@ex3", "@q3", "@s3", "@speed3", "@frequency3", "@then", "@eq3", "@thus3", "@eq4", "@eq5"]}]}